  "verdict": "USABLE \u2014 separates precision on ground truth at the sealed operating point",
  "FPR_probe_level_95pct_upper_bound": 0.0075,
  "fpr_interpretation": "0 false positives observed in 400 control probe-comparisons. By the rule of three the one-sided 95% upper bound on the true probe-level FPR is ~0.0075 (0.75%). This is an UPPER BOUND from a null observation \u2014 it is NOT a demonstration that the true rate is zero.",
  "honest_limits": [
    "only 10 control pairs \u2014 the pairwise FPR is coarse; the probe-level rate (n=400) is the statistically meaningful one",
    "ground truth is ONE model family on ONE GPU class; generalization across families/hardware is untested",
    "fp8 here is KV-cache quantization (vLLM supports fp8 KV; int8/int4 KV are not), while int4 is a different AWQ weight checkpoint \u2014 these are different KINDS of precision change and are reported separately, never pooled",
    "the fp8-KV arm FAILED to boot (documented gotcha: fp8 KV needs an nvcc/CUDA-devel image), so TPR is established for int4 weight-quantization ONLY. A detector that catches a 4-bit weight swap need not catch a subtler KV-precision change \u2014 do NOT generalize the TPR.",
    "the control arms being EXACTLY identical also means this ground truth cannot tell us how the detector behaves against a provider whose backend is merely NOISY rather than substituted"
  ],
  "AUDIT_F4_RESOLUTION_20260722": {
    "prior_defects_and_their_status": {
      "sealed control_pairs_min=10 vs realized 6": "RESOLVED \u2014 a 5th fp16 arm was added; C(5,2) = 10 control pairs now SATISFIES the seal as written.",
      "held-out FPR was 0 by arithmetic (all control D tied at 0.0)": "RESOLVED \u2014 the control D values are no longer tied ([0.0, 0.025]), so leave-one-pair-out is a real comparison rather than '0 > 0' repeated.",
      "tau = 0 was degenerate (zero margin; one differing probe triggered a detection)": "RESOLVED \u2014 tau is now 0.025, derived from the SAME sealed rule applied to real control spread. It was not chosen after seeing results.",
      "'zero observed' FPR overstated precision": "RESOLVED \u2014 the probe-level FPR is now a genuine NON-ZERO measured rate (0.01) over 400 comparisons, not a zero requiring a rule-of-three bound to interpret.",
      "TPR covered int4 WEIGHT quantization only (the fp8-KV arm failed to boot)": "RESOLVED \u2014 the fp8-KV arm booted on a CUDA-devel image and is DETECTED at D = 1.0 (40/40 probes differing), so TPR now covers a KV-PRECISION substitution as well as a weight substitution. The 'do NOT generalize beyond int4' caveat is lifted for fp8 KV specifically."
    },
    "what_the_5th_arm_also_revealed": "fp16_r4 (batch_pad=16) differs from EVERY other fp16 arm on 1 of 40 probes. That is a genuine top-1 flip caused by CO-BATCH COMPOSITION at temperature 0 -- the first such observation in this repo, and it bears directly on the determinism work (see results/data/determinism/batch_divergence_hunt.json). CAVEAT: these arms vary seed AND batch_pad together; at temperature-0 greedy decoding seed should not matter, but this is ONE observation and not a controlled attribution.",
    "remaining_honest_limits": [
      "TPR still rests on ONE arm-pair per positive condition (fp8-KV and int4-AWQ), not a distribution.",
      "One model family, one GPU class, one engine build.",
      "Greedy decoding only; says nothing about sampled decoding.",
      "This is self-hosted ground truth and supports NO claim about any commercial provider."
    ]
  },
  "honesty_tag": "F4 defects RESOLVED by a real re-run \u2014 seal satisfied, tautology broken, 2 positive arms"
